Q3VL Path B (HIP shuffle-write variant): serve the MXFP4 Qwen3-VL-235B model
with a contiguous shuffle-layout paged KV cache end-to-end.

Depends on 0009 (q3vl fused attn prologue) being applied first. This patch does
NOT swap to FlyDSL -- it keeps the precompiled HIP op
``fused_qk_norm_mrope_3d_cache_pts_quant_shuffle`` and merely flips its
``use_shuffle_layout`` arg False->True, plus the matching allocation + read
changes so write and read agree on the shuffle byte arrangement. The change is
value-preserving (same quantized values, different in-block byte order), so it
isolates the layout effect from any kernel/rounding change.

Change set (all verified against image mlperf6.1-q3vl-imgR-r723-vllm251-20260724
and /opt/aiter):

1. get_kv_cache_shape -> kv-first, per-half-contiguous
   (2, num_blocks, num_kv_heads, head_size, block_size). unbind(0) then yields
   two genuinely contiguous halves (num_blocks, num_kv_heads, head_size,
   block_size), each an exact contiguous reshape into the aiter fp8 shuffle
   layouts K [nb,H,D/x,bs,x] / V [nb,H,bs/x,D,x] (x=16). Byte count and
   page_size_bytes are unchanged (page_size_bytes is computed independently from
   block_size*num_kv_heads*head_size*dtype in kv_cache_interface.py), so memory
   profiling / available-KV / block allocation are unaffected.

   get_kv_cache_block_dim is NOT overridden: the base class derives it as
   shape.index(num_blocks) == 1 for the new shape, which is correct. For a pure
   decoder on a single backend (Qwen3-VL), _has_mixed_attention_kv_layout is
   False and there is no mamba, so _update_hybrid_attention_mamba_layout never
   runs and the kv-first layout is NOT renormalized to blocks-first.

2. _split_kv_cache -> unbind(0), view fp8, reshape each half to the 5-D shuffle
   layout. The write kernel reads k_cache.stride(0) (== num_kv_heads*head_size*
   block_size for the contiguous 5-D half) as its per-block stride; the read
   (unified_attention shuffled_kv_cache=True, fp8 branch) parses shapes as
   num_blocks, num_kv_heads, _, block_size, K_WIDTH = k.shape.

3. forward -> pass shuffled_kv_cache=True to the aiter unified_attention call
   (keyword arg, default False, threaded into the 2D/3D kernels per patch 0026).

4. 0009 writer (qwen3_moe.py) -> use_shuffle_layout True; derive block_size from
   the raw kv-first allocation (kv_cache.shape[-1]) instead of key_cache.shape[1]
   (which is now num_kv_heads under the 5-D split view).

